WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.716 --> 00:00:13.777
was the last day of school before Thanksgiving vacation.

2
00:00:14.798 --> 00:00:16.718
And Nina was already feeling thankful.

3
00:00:17.759 --> 00:00:20.280
Her teacher hadn't given the class any homework!

4
00:00:23.541 --> 00:00:26.563
At Kids Central Izzie was wearing an Indian headdress.

5
00:00:27.623 --> 00:00:29.084
She made it in art class.

6
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.742
"I am thankful that Indians taught us how to eat corn.

7
00:00:34.803 --> 00:00:35.904
I love corn."

8
00:00:36.945 --> 00:00:37.985
She bounced around.

9
00:00:42.529 --> 00:00:44.350
And I'm thankful for pretty flowers!"

10
00:00:46.432 --> 00:00:49.894
Miss Shelly was carrying two large vases filled with flowers.

11
00:00:49.914 --> 00:00:52.476
"Are those for our activity?"

12
00:00:52.856 --> 00:00:54.758
Nina asked, hoping they were.

13
00:00:56.399 --> 00:00:57.360
Miss Shelly nodded.

14
00:00:58.368 --> 00:01:01.190
"The end of autumn means the end of fresh flowers.

15
00:01:03.512 --> 00:01:06.193
We're going to press these flowers and let them dry.

16
00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:09.296
In a few weeks, they'll be ready to use."

17
00:01:09.316 --> 00:01:12.698
"How will we use them?"

18
00:01:13.098 --> 00:01:13.919
Nina asked.

19
00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.422
"You can use them to make cards," Miss Shelly said.

20
00:01:18.442 --> 00:01:23.605
"Today I brought some flowers that I pressed last month.

21
00:01:24.726 --> 00:01:27.168
After we press flowers, we'll make thank you cards."

22
00:01:28.396 --> 00:01:30.417
"Thanksgiving thank you cards?"

23
00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:31.577
Bobby asked.

24
00:01:31.597 --> 00:01:35.478
"Yes," Miss Shelly answered.

25
00:01:35.498 --> 00:01:39.479
"While we're working, think of someone you'd like to thank.

26
00:01:40.639 --> 00:01:43.280
Right now, choose four flowers you'd like to press."

27
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.761
Nina leaned over the orange, yellow, and red flowers.

28
00:01:48.862 --> 00:01:50.702
Everyone else quickly grabbed theirs.

29
00:01:51.802 --> 00:01:53.683
But the flowers were all so pretty.

30
00:01:54.603 --> 00:01:55.743
It was hard to choose.

31
00:01:55.763 --> 00:01:58.497
"Nina, are you ready?"

32
00:01:59.437 --> 00:02:00.558
Miss Shelly was waiting.

33
00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:05.242
Nina closed her eyes and pulled out four flowers.

34
00:02:07.364 --> 00:02:10.206
Then Miss Shelly started showing them how to press flowers.

35
00:02:10.226 --> 00:02:14.289
"Take one piece of paper and fold it in half.

36
00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:18.613
Open it back up, and arrange your flowers on the inside.

37
00:02:19.714 --> 00:02:21.695
Make sure the flowers don't touch each other.

38
00:02:22.796 --> 00:02:24.177
Then fold it shut again."

39
00:02:24.197 --> 00:02:30.573
"Cute. It's like a little flower book," Nina said.

40
00:02:30.593 --> 00:02:34.294
"Now take one of these giant dictionaries."

41
00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.575
Miss Shelly held up a fat dictionary.

42
00:02:37.595 --> 00:02:41.156
"The dictionary will press our flowers for us."

43
00:02:41.176 --> 00:02:45.237
"Turn to the very last page of the dictionary.

44
00:02:45.997 --> 00:02:50.678
We're going to put your little flower book in between the last page and the back cover.

45
00:02:52.439 --> 00:02:56.980
In a few weeks, you'll have beautiful pressed flowers," Miss Shelly said.

46
00:02:58.108 --> 00:03:00.810
Nina followed Miss Shelly's directions exactly.

47
00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.231
Nina hoped her flowers would come out pretty.

48
00:03:04.251 --> 00:03:08.194
"Did you decide who you'd like to thank?"

49
00:03:08.594 --> 00:03:09.574
Miss Shelly asked.

50
00:03:10.515 --> 00:03:12.176
She opened a red tin box.

51
00:03:13.196 --> 00:03:15.237
She lifted out stacks of cardboard.

52
00:03:16.338 --> 00:03:19.740
Nina saw sheets of pressed flowers between the cardboard.

53
00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.962
Miss Shelly gave them blank cards.

54
00:03:22.982 --> 00:03:27.124
"Once you've written your card, brush glue on the front.

55
00:03:28.168 --> 00:03:31.370
Then choose some pressed flowers to gently place on top.

56
00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:35.292
In a few weeks, the flowers you pressed today will be dry.

57
00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:38.514
Then you can make cards like these at home."

58
00:03:44.097 --> 00:03:45.397
Nina looked at Miss Shelly.

59
00:03:45.417 --> 00:03:48.039
"Who is your thank you card for?"

60
00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.340
Miss Shelly paused.

61
00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.022
"My mother," she said.

62
00:03:53.042 --> 00:03:54.722
"What about you?"

63
00:03:55.743 --> 00:03:57.184
Nina smiled shyly.

64
00:03:58.236 --> 00:04:00.217
"It's a secret," she said.

65
00:04:04.879 --> 00:04:05.259
to go!

66
00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:11.702
Nina, don't forget your card," Miss Shelly called.

67
00:04:11.722 --> 00:04:16.404
"I made it for you," Nina told her teacher.

68
00:04:22.046 --> 00:04:23.526
Miss Shelly opened the card.

69
00:04:25.047 --> 00:04:31.479
It said: "Dear Miss Shelly, Thank you for 238 days of fun at Kids Central.

70
00:04:32.542 --> 00:04:33.605
Happy Thanksgiving!

71
00:04:34.708 --> 00:04:35.089
Love,
